WEBVTT

00:56.198 --> 00:58.868
FILING FOR LOVE

01:06.750 --> 01:08.043
Hello, everyone.

01:08.669 --> 01:12.256
I'm Park A-jeong, VP Jeon Jae-yeol's
former executive assistant.

01:15.176 --> 01:17.178
Your secretary? What on earth...

01:17.261 --> 01:18.429
What is all this?

01:19.805 --> 01:21.140
What trick are you pulling again?

01:21.223 --> 01:22.641
It's not a trick, Father.

01:22.725 --> 01:25.811
She made the brave call
to take a stand for our company.

01:26.270 --> 01:29.190
Are all Haemu shareholder meetings
this haphazard and unplanned?

01:30.191 --> 01:32.193
Do you allow just anyone
to stand and speak?

01:32.276 --> 01:35.988
I'm here because the shareholders
have a right to know.

01:36.530 --> 01:40.242
Only shareholders
are allowed to speak at...

01:47.875 --> 01:51.795
According to the report
I'm holding in my hand

01:52.129 --> 01:55.466
when VP Jeon Jae-yeol
was CEO of Haemu Pharmaceutical

01:55.549 --> 01:57.510
he transferred billions of won
without authorization

01:57.593 --> 01:59.970
to the medical foundation
he established.

02:00.262 --> 02:03.057
However, no audit was carried out.
Actually...

02:03.140 --> 02:04.850
it was practically impossible.

02:05.184 --> 02:06.352
That's because

02:06.435 --> 02:10.147
Joo In-a, the Head of Audit,
who was responsible for investigating

02:10.648 --> 02:12.608
covered up the transfers.

02:18.697 --> 02:21.116
Do you admit to it, Ms. Joo?

02:37.925 --> 02:41.136
It's true that Haemu Pharmaceutical
donated to Jei Medical Foundation.

02:42.763 --> 02:46.684
But I concluded there were
no issues with legal proceedings.

02:46.767 --> 02:48.644
Just because you conclude
that there are no issues

02:48.727 --> 02:50.437
does that mean
you don't have to conduct an audit?

02:51.855 --> 02:53.607
Auditing is about risk management.

02:54.191 --> 02:56.569
I judged that the risk
of conducting the audit

02:56.819 --> 02:59.822
was greater than the risk
of not conducting it.

02:59.905 --> 03:01.574
OH HYUN-YOUNG
JEON JAE-YEOL

03:02.575 --> 03:05.744
Political and cliquish factions exist
within Haemu regarding succession.

03:06.620 --> 03:10.541
I thought the investigation
would become politically charged

03:10.624 --> 03:13.460
putting Haemu
into even worse turmoil.

03:13.544 --> 03:15.588
My point is

03:16.005 --> 03:18.674
who gives you
the right to decide that?

03:18.757 --> 03:20.843
It's my job to make such decisions.

03:21.093 --> 03:23.929
How can we trust Ms. Joo's decision?

03:24.263 --> 03:26.974
VP Jeon Jae-yeol
and Head of Audit Joo In-a

03:27.057 --> 03:28.392
were in a romantic relationship.

03:29.476 --> 03:33.522
Was Ms. Joo's decision based
solely on the company's interests?

03:33.981 --> 03:35.649
What if she made that choice

03:36.233 --> 03:37.901
for VP Jeon Jae-yeol's sake?

03:41.488 --> 03:43.907
Goodness, what on earth
is all this about?

03:46.243 --> 03:47.578
Why didn't you do anything?

03:48.746 --> 03:51.165
What were you doing while the company
ended up in this state?

03:52.833 --> 03:53.834
- Father.
- Sir.

03:54.001 --> 03:55.085
- Father.
- Father.

03:55.169 --> 03:56.253
Are you all right?

03:56.503 --> 03:57.755
- Oh, no.
- Father!

03:57.838 --> 03:59.757
At the Haemu Group
shareholder meeting held today

03:59.840 --> 04:02.092
allegations surfaced
that the Head of Audit covered up

04:02.176 --> 04:05.220
VP Jeon Jae-yeol's misconduct,
sparking major controversy.

04:05.929 --> 04:10.517
Haemu Group President Jeon Moo-tae
collapsed during the meeting

04:10.601 --> 04:12.478
which was immediately suspended.

04:12.895 --> 04:15.105
Haemu Group convened
an emergency board meeting

04:15.189 --> 04:18.150
to launch a wide-scale investigation
into the allegations.

04:18.692 --> 04:21.779
With concerns
over both the chairman's health

04:21.862 --> 04:25.032
and management ethics intensifying

04:25.115 --> 04:29.328
Haemu Group's succession battle
has again fallen into turmoil.

04:42.341 --> 04:44.802
Gosh, with the company in this mess

04:45.135 --> 04:47.221
I could barely swallow my food.

04:47.304 --> 04:48.972
You emptied your bowl today.

04:49.223 --> 04:50.599
Goodness gracious.

04:50.683 --> 04:53.477
I heard the basement press room
filled up after the news came out.

04:54.395 --> 04:57.022
It looks like
all the journalists are here.

04:57.940 --> 05:01.318
I think it's drawing more attention
because of the VP's scandal.

05:01.777 --> 05:04.113
Ms. Joo's personal information is
already all over the internet.

05:04.321 --> 05:06.448
Oh, gosh. Guys.

05:06.532 --> 05:08.784
Let's watch what we say in public.

05:08.867 --> 05:12.121
If your wife or boyfriend asks,
just say you don't know anything.

05:12.204 --> 05:13.747
- We never know how it'll spread.
- Okay.

05:13.831 --> 05:15.666
It's true
we don't really know anything.

05:16.875 --> 05:19.044
About Ms. Park's report...

05:19.128 --> 05:20.587
How much of it do you think is true?

05:20.921 --> 05:23.716
If someone like Ms. Joo covered it up

05:23.799 --> 05:27.386
don't you think there's still
something between her and the VP?

05:28.554 --> 05:29.805
There isn't.

05:30.973 --> 05:33.267
How do you know that, Ms. Yoon?

05:33.892 --> 05:36.395
I know who Ms. Joo is dating now.

05:36.562 --> 05:38.856
- What?
- It's not our VP.

05:40.065 --> 05:41.734
- Who is it?
- Who is it?

05:43.652 --> 05:46.572
It's someone we all know.

05:46.655 --> 05:48.490
- Someone we know? Who?
- I don't know anyone.

05:48.574 --> 05:49.742
- What?
- Who is it?

05:50.033 --> 05:51.285
- Who is it?
- Who is it?

05:51.368 --> 05:53.328
- Who is it?
- Yes, who is it? Tell us.

05:53.412 --> 05:55.372
- Take a look around.
- What?

05:55.748 --> 05:57.166
- Come on.
- You can't just walk off.

05:57.249 --> 05:59.168
- You need to tell us.
- What do you know?

05:59.251 --> 06:00.377
- Tell me.
- Talk to us.

06:09.720 --> 06:11.180
HEAD OF AUDIT

06:15.058 --> 06:17.186
They've been keeping her all day.

06:21.356 --> 06:24.359
SPECIAL INVESTIGATION COMMITTEE

06:24.818 --> 06:26.320
State your relationship with VP Jeon

06:26.403 --> 06:28.405
when you reviewed
the Jei Medical Foundation case.

06:28.906 --> 06:30.449
We weren't in any relationship.

06:30.657 --> 06:31.992
You two used to date.

06:32.075 --> 06:33.202
We weren't at the time.

06:33.285 --> 06:35.746
No one who was a couple
goes back to being just strangers.

06:35.829 --> 06:38.791
Could there be any worse relationship
than a couple who broke up?

06:39.792 --> 06:41.210
It's worse off than strangers.

06:42.044 --> 06:44.630
VP Jeon said
he still had feelings for you.

06:44.713 --> 06:45.714
I did not.

06:45.798 --> 06:48.467
Even when you were reviewing
the medical foundation case?

06:50.385 --> 06:51.678
Even then.

06:52.095 --> 06:54.223
Here are Jei Medical Foundation's
shareholding records

06:54.306 --> 06:57.267
meeting minutes of decision-making
processes at Haemu Pharmaceutical

06:57.351 --> 07:00.312
sponsorship approvals,
and fund usage records.

07:01.063 --> 07:02.981
You'll see for yourself
if you read those.

07:03.649 --> 07:05.984
As CEO at the time, I played no part
in running the foundation

07:06.485 --> 07:09.905
nor influenced Haemu Pharmaceutical's
decision-making process.

07:10.239 --> 07:12.574
All funds were used appropriately

07:12.658 --> 07:13.700
within their means.

07:14.409 --> 07:16.912
If there were no issues
in the process

07:17.204 --> 07:19.998
then there was no fault
on Ms. Joo's part to decide

07:20.457 --> 07:21.834
not to investigate.

07:22.292 --> 07:26.213
Whether she was at fault or not
will be decided in court.

07:26.463 --> 07:28.549
There clearly are
grounds for an argument.

07:28.632 --> 07:31.468
I think we should find out
exactly why she didn't look into it.

07:32.636 --> 07:33.846
Don't you think?

07:49.736 --> 07:52.447
It'll be more complicated
than we thought.

07:54.491 --> 07:55.617
What did Joo In-a say?

07:56.034 --> 07:58.871
She's maintaining
that she made an official call.

08:00.539 --> 08:03.125
Why is she still fighting
when we've come this far?

08:05.335 --> 08:06.712
Whether Jae-yeol's guilty or not

08:06.795 --> 08:09.214
won't matter
once news of the scandal gets out.

08:09.298 --> 08:11.008
Bring Joo In-a down at all costs.

08:11.091 --> 08:12.801
- Yes, sir.
- Okay.

08:23.979 --> 08:26.064
I'm with Haesin Daily. Can we talk?

08:26.148 --> 08:27.608
Hello, this is XTM.

08:27.691 --> 08:28.942
Are you available for an interview?

08:29.026 --> 08:30.652
The VP's mistress

08:30.736 --> 08:32.905
- should rot in a pit forever.
- Gosh, it's gross.

08:33.530 --> 08:34.990
Hello, Ms. Joo.

08:36.575 --> 08:37.618
Gosh.

08:38.327 --> 08:39.745
You are a beauty.

08:41.204 --> 08:44.666
Oh, I'm Park Dae-geun
with Daily Hansung.

08:45.292 --> 08:47.377
I have nothing to say. Sorry.

08:48.045 --> 08:50.797
You grew up in Mipo, didn't you?

08:52.507 --> 08:54.301
You were
quite a popular figure there, too.

08:55.427 --> 08:57.220
I heard the smart, pretty girl

08:57.679 --> 09:00.140
grew up in a messed-up family.

09:08.190 --> 09:09.399
Daily Hansung?

09:10.275 --> 09:12.527
You probably didn't know because
you work for a media-like outlet

09:12.611 --> 09:14.279
that just copies social media posts

09:14.905 --> 09:17.282
and writes clickbait articles
without doing real reporting.

09:17.741 --> 09:19.451
This area is restricted to reporters.

09:20.619 --> 09:21.620
Security?

09:22.204 --> 09:23.747
An outsider got in.

09:27.834 --> 09:29.878
- I need you to leave.
- Sorry.

09:30.379 --> 09:31.421
My bad.

09:50.607 --> 09:51.608
Hop in.

10:04.162 --> 10:06.289
Wow, didn't that just feel
like we were filming an action movie?

10:06.999 --> 10:08.583
I'd call it a romance,
not an action film

10:08.667 --> 10:10.127
because I appeared
at just the right moment.

10:10.544 --> 10:12.129
Let's call it a romantic action film.

10:15.048 --> 10:16.591
How do you feel?

10:16.675 --> 10:18.301
It must be hard
being questioned all day long.

10:18.385 --> 10:19.761
It was nothing.

10:20.095 --> 10:22.556
I was a nude model for a long time.

10:22.639 --> 10:23.765
It was not tough one bit.

10:33.525 --> 10:35.068
She said she wasn't tired one bit.

10:44.953 --> 10:46.538
Oh, gosh. I dozed off.

10:49.374 --> 10:50.959
I didn't snore, did I?

10:52.127 --> 10:53.462
You did, actually.

10:57.632 --> 10:58.800
Did I really?

10:59.384 --> 11:00.802
Did I snore?

11:00.886 --> 11:02.763
You're lying, aren't you?

11:04.848 --> 11:06.391
Are you serious?

11:06.475 --> 11:07.976
Did I really snore?

11:08.060 --> 11:10.187
Really? Honestly?
No, I didn't, did I?

11:10.270 --> 11:12.814
Was I really snoring? Seriously?

11:12.898 --> 11:14.066
- Did I...
- You didn't.

11:14.483 --> 11:16.234
You didn't snore. It was a joke.

11:18.570 --> 11:20.822
But you were dead asleep, though.

11:21.198 --> 11:23.200
As soon as you get home

11:23.283 --> 11:25.452
take a shower
then jump right into bed.

11:26.828 --> 11:28.205
You nag too much.

11:28.914 --> 11:29.998
I'll do that.

11:33.001 --> 11:34.336
Drop me off over there.

11:43.011 --> 11:44.262
Thanks for the ride.

11:44.346 --> 11:45.972
Don't get out. Go on home.

11:46.056 --> 11:47.307
No, I'll walk you home first.

11:47.599 --> 11:50.310
You dropped me off.
Now let me see you drive off.

11:50.393 --> 11:51.937
I'll leave
after I see you get inside.

11:52.854 --> 11:54.314
I want to see you off.

11:55.649 --> 11:57.734
Let's do this, then. We'll wave.

11:58.193 --> 12:00.028
Bye. Take care.

12:00.987 --> 12:02.114
Aren't I good at walking backward?

12:08.453 --> 12:09.955
There are reporters
outside your building.

12:46.783 --> 12:47.826
It's freezing cold.

13:12.934 --> 13:14.811
I'll send you some photos.

13:15.353 --> 13:16.688
Look into someone for me.

13:18.356 --> 13:21.776
- If you're done, come out and eat.
- Okay.

13:27.282 --> 13:29.576
It's a bit big, but it works.
How do I look?

13:30.744 --> 13:32.913
It's not too big at all.
You look pretty.

13:36.750 --> 13:40.086
My gosh. What is all this?
It's a total feast.

13:40.170 --> 13:41.963
My sisters came by last weekend.

13:42.380 --> 13:45.759
They made kimchi, so I asked for some
to share with you.

13:45.967 --> 13:48.678
They brought enough food
to fill a whole fridge.

13:48.762 --> 13:51.306
Do people make seasoned cockles
when making kimchi?

13:52.390 --> 13:55.101
No, they brought this
because it's my favorite.

13:55.393 --> 13:57.103
Cockles are hard to clean

13:57.187 --> 13:59.773
so I tell my mom to stop making them,
but she still does it.

14:00.232 --> 14:01.650
She could've made just a little.

14:01.900 --> 14:04.361
She makes way too much,
and I can never eat it all.

14:06.112 --> 14:07.113
Noh Ki-jun.

14:07.739 --> 14:09.991
Your family adores you.

14:11.117 --> 14:12.369
Too much for my liking.

14:12.452 --> 14:14.663
Too much love is a nuisance, too.

14:16.873 --> 14:18.083
What a spoiled thing to say.

14:21.294 --> 14:22.587
Thanks for the food.

14:23.713 --> 14:25.423
What are your sisters like?

14:25.507 --> 14:27.133
I want to hear about them.

14:30.220 --> 14:31.263
My older sisters...

14:34.140 --> 14:36.017
- They're just sisters.
- What?

14:36.101 --> 14:37.394
There's not much to say.

14:38.561 --> 14:39.562
- Oh, wait.
- What?

14:40.355 --> 14:43.775
- My sisters' kids are adorable.
- Let me see.

14:45.652 --> 14:46.653
Here.

14:47.821 --> 14:48.989
That's so cute.

14:55.996 --> 14:57.622
How sweet...

15:19.769 --> 15:21.730
HAEMU'S BROTHERLY STRIFE:
FEMME FATALE AUDITOR AT THE CENTER

15:32.365 --> 15:34.200
Guys, did you all read...

15:38.872 --> 15:39.998
You're reading it.

15:47.088 --> 15:50.842
The Head of Audit is accused
of an affair with VP Jeon Jae-yeol.

15:51.676 --> 15:53.553
Does infidelity run in her family?

15:54.554 --> 15:58.558
It's worth noting Joo was born
from an extramarital affair.

15:59.434 --> 16:02.187
But the string of men surrounding her
who shook an entire corporation

16:02.270 --> 16:03.730
doesn't end here.

16:04.522 --> 16:05.607
According to my research...

16:05.690 --> 16:08.568
"It has been confirmed
that she is dating Noh

16:08.651 --> 16:11.363
one of her subordinates
in the Audit Team."

16:12.030 --> 16:15.116
What's even more shocking is that
Noh was in charge of investigating

16:15.200 --> 16:16.493
the Haemu Pharmaceutical case

16:17.369 --> 16:20.663
that's at the center
of the controversy."

16:25.001 --> 16:27.670
We could get something
if we piece this together nicely.

16:28.463 --> 16:31.966
I was getting annoyed
at how things were dragging on.

16:48.024 --> 16:49.025
HAEMU'S BROTHERLY STRIFE

16:49.109 --> 16:50.110
Mr. Noh.

16:51.319 --> 16:54.280
Is this article about you?
That you're her lover?

16:56.324 --> 16:58.868
What's this about Ms. Joo
being born out of wedlock?

17:00.495 --> 17:02.122
The reporter went way over the line.

17:04.457 --> 17:06.876
Mr. Noh, where are you going?

17:17.470 --> 17:19.180
I swear, it's the truth.

17:19.264 --> 17:20.265
- No way.
- No way.

17:20.348 --> 17:22.475
Come on. I confirmed it.

17:22.559 --> 17:23.560
Are you sure?

17:24.644 --> 17:27.689
The two went
into Noh's place at night.

17:28.773 --> 17:30.191
She was there for a long time.

17:30.275 --> 17:31.901
That's a scoop.

17:31.985 --> 17:34.446
- What?
- Was she really born out of wedlock?

17:34.529 --> 17:36.364
A friend of mine is from Mipo.

17:36.448 --> 17:38.741
The mother and daughter duo
were social outcasts.

17:38.825 --> 17:39.868
Oh, dear...

17:40.785 --> 17:43.580
"The poor Head of Audit
who followed in her parents' steps."

17:44.622 --> 17:45.915
Isn't that hilarious?

17:45.999 --> 17:47.459
You could turn it into a movie.

17:50.170 --> 17:51.546
Watch what you say.

17:53.214 --> 17:54.215
Oh, my gosh.

17:55.717 --> 17:57.886
- This is Mr. Noh Ki-jun.
- I see.

17:59.929 --> 18:01.097
Does being a reporter

18:01.431 --> 18:03.641
give you the right to print
one's personal business

18:03.725 --> 18:05.435
and gossip about it in the open?

18:05.894 --> 18:06.895
What's with that glare?

18:07.437 --> 18:08.605
Do you want to punch me?

18:08.688 --> 18:10.231
She isn't someone

18:14.152 --> 18:16.362
the likes of you
can talk about so recklessly.

18:22.535 --> 18:23.745
Is this true love?

18:24.496 --> 18:26.331
She was with you for a long time.

18:30.877 --> 18:32.879
Did you punch me? Did you see that?

18:32.962 --> 18:34.297
- Yes.
- You saw that?

18:34.380 --> 18:35.715
Did you see him punch me first?

18:35.798 --> 18:37.509
- Yes.
- Have you lost your mind?

18:38.635 --> 18:39.636
Hey, you.

18:42.680 --> 18:45.308
So what if you're a reporter?

18:46.684 --> 18:47.727
- Oh, no.
- Stop him.

18:47.810 --> 18:49.062
- Get him off him.
- Gosh.

18:54.526 --> 18:56.986
BOO SE-YOUNG, HEAD OF HR

18:57.070 --> 18:58.988
What is this? Is this for real?

19:02.075 --> 19:04.202
HAEMU'S BROTHERLY STRIFE,
FEMME FATALE AUDITOR AT THE CENTER

19:05.453 --> 19:07.121
You're the one who told me

19:08.373 --> 19:10.959
to take a good look
at who's really falling apart.

19:12.710 --> 19:14.837
Who do you think that is?

19:15.880 --> 19:19.342
I don't think it's you or me

19:19.676 --> 19:21.594
or even Jeon Jae-yeol.

19:22.679 --> 19:26.015
Ki-jun seems to be
the one who's falling apart.

19:30.228 --> 19:31.354
What are you saying?

19:31.646 --> 19:35.066
Jeon Sung-yeol plans to stick
the foundation case on Ki-jun.

19:35.608 --> 19:39.195
He'll make it look like Jeon Jae-yeol
ordered your team to cover it up.

19:39.696 --> 19:41.030
That would be the cleanest outcome.

19:43.575 --> 19:45.034
I find that silly.

19:45.618 --> 19:48.329
How could Ki-jun and Jeon Jae-yeol
be accomplices?

19:50.206 --> 19:51.332
Hang on.

19:52.584 --> 19:53.710
Maybe they are accomplices

19:54.836 --> 19:57.380
in loving the same woman to death.

19:58.464 --> 19:59.549
Is that it?

20:03.595 --> 20:04.804
You don't seem to get it.

20:05.513 --> 20:07.140
The word "accomplice"

20:07.724 --> 20:10.101
refers to you and Jeon Sung-yeol.

20:11.144 --> 20:13.104
You frame people
by twisting facts and exaggerating

20:13.187 --> 20:14.647
to turn someone into a scapegoat.

20:16.149 --> 20:17.900
People who conspire to do such things

20:19.319 --> 20:20.987
are called accomplices.

20:22.405 --> 20:24.240
All you did by siding
with Jeon Sung-yeol

20:24.782 --> 20:27.910
was bring down the friend
who helped you when you were in need.

20:29.871 --> 20:31.331
Was that your plan, too?

20:33.833 --> 20:35.668
Not only did you ruin
Jeon Jae-yeol's life

20:36.336 --> 20:39.339
but you're the type who brings
trouble to people around you.

20:40.590 --> 20:42.717
Do you even know Ki-jun
is at the police station?

20:43.718 --> 20:46.429
He assaulted the journalist
who exposed you.

20:53.311 --> 20:54.437
Settle?

20:54.520 --> 20:57.899
I have no intention of settling.
That's final.

20:58.191 --> 21:01.277
Check the CCTV and witnesses
and see who punched whom first.

21:01.361 --> 21:03.905
He attacked me,
and I was only defending myself.

21:04.322 --> 21:06.074
Sure. Whatever.

21:06.157 --> 21:07.867
I won't settle, either.

21:08.034 --> 21:12.955
Oh, and I'll sue this guy here
for defamation.

21:13.039 --> 21:16.042
He brought up someone's personal life
that's unrelated to the case

21:16.125 --> 21:17.919
to write a malicious piece.

21:18.002 --> 21:21.089
"Malicious"?
How dare you call it that?

21:21.381 --> 21:25.718
Using personal details
to paint a nice story is what I do!

21:25.802 --> 21:28.805
- It's in the public interest!
- "Public interest"?

21:30.139 --> 21:32.016
How is that public interest?

21:33.685 --> 21:38.940
She's not someone you can define
with a few lines of journalism.

21:39.023 --> 21:42.777
The kind of life she had,
how she fought to survive

21:43.194 --> 21:46.447
what choices she had made,
and how those choices tormented her

21:47.365 --> 21:49.450
were all taken out of context.

21:51.202 --> 21:55.248
You made a spectacle of her wounds,
and you call that...

21:56.708 --> 21:59.711
What kind of public interest is that?

22:02.130 --> 22:03.297
Goodness.

22:04.340 --> 22:05.717
You must like her a lot.

22:08.052 --> 22:10.054
Yes, I like her a lot.

22:10.471 --> 22:12.140
Because she's a good person.

22:13.349 --> 22:15.727
You can scorn and mock all you want

22:16.978 --> 22:18.938
but you'll never hurt her.

22:20.440 --> 22:22.900
I know who she truly is

22:24.402 --> 22:26.154
and I'll protect her until the end.

22:30.783 --> 22:32.034
I'm not making any settlements.

22:52.597 --> 22:53.765
Ms. Joo?

22:56.100 --> 22:57.185
What the...

22:57.393 --> 22:58.561
You startled me.

23:00.438 --> 23:01.647
Have some tofu.

23:07.945 --> 23:10.281
- Does it hurt?
- Yes, be gentle.

23:13.785 --> 23:15.244
Don't be a drama queen.

23:15.953 --> 23:19.540
I have thin and soft skin.
That's why.

23:19.624 --> 23:21.250
If you're that frail and soft

23:21.501 --> 23:23.044
why would you go around
punching people?

23:23.127 --> 23:26.130
Do you think you're a kid?
Why would you get into a fight?

23:32.094 --> 23:33.262
You did well.

23:33.846 --> 23:35.223
I felt great.

23:35.306 --> 23:37.475
I should've been the one
to teach him a lesson.

23:38.935 --> 23:42.772
Reporter Park was really lucky.

23:43.147 --> 23:46.067
He should be glad
I'm the one who beat him up.

23:47.985 --> 23:50.196
Take a pill to make sure
this doesn't fester before bed.

23:50.446 --> 23:51.864
- Okay?
- What?

23:53.658 --> 23:54.700
Wait.

23:56.035 --> 23:57.036
Hey.

24:00.331 --> 24:01.332
Are you leaving?

24:02.416 --> 24:04.001
I should. I have my own place.

24:04.377 --> 24:05.753
It's really cold out.

24:05.837 --> 24:07.964
I drove here.
I'll put the heater on full blast.

24:08.047 --> 24:10.132
It's late. You might
doze off at the wheel.

24:10.216 --> 24:11.384
I'm perfectly fine.

24:11.467 --> 24:13.427
Don't you worry and sleep well.

24:13.511 --> 24:14.512
See you.

24:16.430 --> 24:17.932
I have a tree.

24:20.935 --> 24:23.688
Shall we decorate my Christmas tree?

24:25.982 --> 24:28.526
You have a Christmas tree at home?

24:46.752 --> 24:48.754
Wow, it's beautiful.

24:55.636 --> 24:56.888
You know

24:57.388 --> 24:58.973
this is the first time
I've put up a Christmas tree.

24:59.432 --> 25:00.474
Really?

25:00.683 --> 25:03.519
- Didn't you have one at home?
- No.

25:04.270 --> 25:07.064
I had no room for anything sparkly.

25:11.402 --> 25:12.445
From now on

25:13.154 --> 25:14.530
we'll do this together every year.

25:16.490 --> 25:20.119
We should hang gems next year
like gold and silver trinkets.

25:20.745 --> 25:21.787
Gold is too expensive now.

25:22.163 --> 25:25.875
I even got a star for you.
Getting gold will be a piece of cake.

25:27.668 --> 25:30.630
You're right.
I also prefer gold to a star.

25:31.797 --> 25:32.840
I knew it.

25:37.470 --> 25:38.679
It's so pretty.

25:56.781 --> 25:57.782
INCOMING CALL

25:59.742 --> 26:01.118
Hello, Joo In-a speaking.

26:01.661 --> 26:04.372
Hello, I'm Ki-jun's big sister.

26:09.543 --> 26:12.088
New articles and comments
keep coming up

26:12.880 --> 26:15.091
but Ki-jun won't take
any of our calls.

26:16.592 --> 26:19.220
Even if we were to get through
and ask about it

26:19.637 --> 26:22.348
I don't think he'd tell us anything.

26:23.432 --> 26:24.809
We tried...

26:27.228 --> 26:29.647
We couldn't take it. So here we are.

26:30.648 --> 26:31.774
I see.

26:32.316 --> 26:33.651
What kind of person

26:34.402 --> 26:35.736
are you really?

26:37.321 --> 26:38.656
- Pardon?
- Well...

26:39.031 --> 26:42.076
You nursed our Ki-jun back to health

26:42.368 --> 26:45.579
so we assumed you two
had feelings for each other.

26:47.415 --> 26:51.544
There's talk that you're
the VP's mistress or something...

26:52.044 --> 26:53.129
The heck...

26:54.714 --> 26:56.841
We're not here to start a fight.

26:57.800 --> 27:01.470
As Ki-jun's family,
we want to know the facts.

27:03.180 --> 27:06.434
Our mom took to her bed because
she couldn't handle the shock.

27:06.809 --> 27:10.730
- We didn't know what to tell her.
- Ms. Joo.

27:11.230 --> 27:13.399
What happens to Ki-jun now?

27:14.275 --> 27:15.901
From what we read online

27:15.985 --> 27:18.487
he punched the journalist
who wrote about you.

27:18.571 --> 27:19.780
Is that true?

27:19.864 --> 27:21.449
Our Ki-jun

27:21.532 --> 27:25.578
never got into a fight growing up.

27:25.786 --> 27:28.414
Why would he suddenly...
My heart might explode.

27:28.497 --> 27:32.209
Is something
actually going on at work?

27:32.501 --> 27:36.380
Will Ki-jun
get penalized or something?

27:38.299 --> 27:39.550
Ms. Joo?

27:40.342 --> 27:42.720
You're Ki-jun's superior as well.

27:43.220 --> 27:44.889
Is there something

27:45.681 --> 27:49.810
you could do to help him?

28:05.117 --> 28:08.162
Hand in your company ID
while the investigation's ongoing.

28:27.973 --> 28:29.141
Hey, Ki-jun.

28:29.767 --> 28:30.893
Have you heard?

28:31.310 --> 28:32.812
So I'm going upstairs
to be interviewed.

28:32.895 --> 28:34.355
I called in case you got worried.

28:35.272 --> 28:36.273
Okay.

28:37.191 --> 28:39.151
I'm fine, so don't worry.

28:40.069 --> 28:42.196
Let's get something nice to eat
after I'm done.

28:43.114 --> 28:46.117
Sure. We can do that.
What do you want to eat?

28:48.285 --> 28:49.411
A toasted sandwich?

28:50.037 --> 28:52.915
Let's eat
that toasted sandwich again.

28:55.292 --> 28:56.961
You're eating that all the time.

29:00.673 --> 29:01.674
Ki-jun.

29:03.300 --> 29:04.301
Yes?

29:05.761 --> 29:07.930
No matter what I say from now on

29:08.472 --> 29:10.307
it means that I love you.

29:13.686 --> 29:14.895
My heart skipped a beat.

29:15.771 --> 29:16.772
I know you love me.

29:17.773 --> 29:18.816
I love you, too.

29:19.441 --> 29:21.360
So don't ever feel hurt.

29:45.301 --> 29:47.469
Ms. Joo, what brings you to...

29:51.682 --> 29:53.058
- What's this?
- What's going on?

29:55.978 --> 29:57.146
- Did she lock the door?
- What?

29:57.730 --> 29:58.981
- What's this?
- What's up with her?

30:00.441 --> 30:01.984
- What's this about?
- Joo In-a?

30:06.197 --> 30:07.406
Hello.

30:08.449 --> 30:10.743
I'm Joo In-a,
Haemu Group's Head of Audit.

30:10.826 --> 30:14.371
I'm here to explain where I stand
regarding the many suspicions.

30:17.082 --> 30:19.710
Will you make a statement
about yesterday's article?

30:19.793 --> 30:22.004
Is it true
that you're dating your subordinate?

30:22.087 --> 30:24.298
Did you really cover up
the VP's corruption?

30:25.132 --> 30:28.302
It's not true that a certain employee
covered up the corruption.

30:28.844 --> 30:33.557
Mr. Noh actually raised concerns
about the matter under suspicion.

30:33.807 --> 30:35.976
Why was there no investigation?

30:40.272 --> 30:41.899
I put a stop to it.

30:44.944 --> 30:46.570
I abused my authority.

30:47.196 --> 30:50.532
I told the employee
not to do anything.

30:52.660 --> 30:54.328
He was just being used

30:54.828 --> 30:55.829
by me.

30:56.163 --> 30:57.748
Why did you give such an instruction?

30:57.831 --> 31:01.085
Why did you use your subordinate
to cover up a case?

31:03.087 --> 31:05.464
I did so to protect VP Jeon Jae-yeol.

31:08.175 --> 31:12.012
My personal feelings clouded
my judgment as Head of Audit.

31:12.638 --> 31:15.683
I will take
full responsibility for it.

31:15.766 --> 31:16.767
I apologize.

31:16.850 --> 31:18.978
What do you mean
by "personal feelings"?

31:19.103 --> 31:21.730
Are you admitting
to your affair with the VP?

31:35.244 --> 31:37.830
3 MONTHS LATER

32:20.831 --> 32:21.957
FORWARDER: SAEMUN INTERNATIONAL

32:22.041 --> 32:23.917
VOLUME ERROR

32:31.842 --> 32:35.054
Look at her
staring fiercely at everything.

32:35.346 --> 32:36.805
That's why people call her
the human scanner.

32:37.348 --> 32:38.807
You can tell
that she was in the Audit Team.

32:39.058 --> 32:41.727
Did you see her picking out a fault
with a shipment to Europe last week?

32:42.019 --> 32:44.438
So people who are good at their job
are good no matter where they are.

32:44.521 --> 32:45.981
She surely is competent.

32:46.065 --> 32:48.025
That must be why
the vice president fell for her.

33:01.455 --> 33:03.123
That was the seventh time today.

33:03.207 --> 33:04.375
DIMENSION RECOGNITION ERROR

33:05.042 --> 33:06.543
It's definitely on the rise.

33:10.714 --> 33:15.594
MARCH 3RD, 2026
7 DIMENSION RECOGNITION ERRORS

33:27.022 --> 33:29.817
Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected to voicemail.

33:29.900 --> 33:32.111
After the beep,
you will be charged...

33:34.279 --> 33:38.575
EXCLUSIVE: THE PROSECUTION
FINDS JEON JAE-YEOL OF HAEMU

33:38.659 --> 33:43.414
FREE FROM ALL SUSPICION
INCLUDING PROFESSIONAL NEGLIGENCE

33:56.343 --> 33:58.053
Who told you
it was okay to go ahead with this?

33:59.054 --> 34:01.140
You need to file a planning report
before doing this.

34:01.932 --> 34:04.643
Audit Team Three handles matters
that come through reports

34:05.185 --> 34:06.895
so it is hard to file
a planning report each time.

34:06.979 --> 34:08.689
Who told you it had to be every time?

34:09.064 --> 34:11.316
This is Sales Team One
we're talking about.

34:11.483 --> 34:14.153
Don't you know that the head,
Mr. Cheon, is the immediate junior

34:14.236 --> 34:15.696
of VP Jeon Sung-yeol?

34:15.779 --> 34:17.948
I decided that an investigation
was necessary in the process

34:18.031 --> 34:20.534
of confirming the authenticity
of the report, and...

34:20.617 --> 34:23.162
And who are you to decide?

34:24.746 --> 34:26.457
- Leader of Team Three.
- Yes, sir.

34:26.832 --> 34:28.000
Come over here.

34:28.417 --> 34:30.043
- Right now?
- Yes.

34:31.378 --> 34:32.463
Yes, sure.

34:35.632 --> 34:38.469
Goodness. I never thought

34:38.969 --> 34:42.139
I'd stick around doing this job
long enough to miss Ms. Joo.

34:42.222 --> 34:43.390
Tell me about it.

34:43.932 --> 34:47.227
Ms. Joo also yelled at us,
but everything she said was right.

34:47.311 --> 34:51.273
But now, everything in the Audit Team
has become political.

34:51.815 --> 34:53.567
I hear it's all the same
in other departments, too.

34:53.650 --> 34:56.862
The entire business
is under Jeon Sung-yeol's reign.

34:56.945 --> 34:59.198
Good grief.
What is happening to this company?

34:59.740 --> 35:01.325
Good work, Mr. Noh.

35:01.408 --> 35:03.368
You must be feeling down,
so why don't we grab a drink?

35:03.619 --> 35:05.329
- He's not here.
- What?

35:05.954 --> 35:09.416
He ran out
as soon as the clock hit six o'clock.

35:09.791 --> 35:10.834
Again?

35:10.918 --> 35:12.920
Where has he been going
in such a hurry lately?

35:13.253 --> 35:16.924
Let him be. He wouldn't want to be
in the office even for a second.

35:17.007 --> 35:20.093
People still gossip about Ms. Joo,
both online and offline.

35:21.303 --> 35:23.013
It's a wonder
that he didn't quit his job.

35:23.096 --> 35:25.849
Ms. Joo was really cruel back then.

35:25.933 --> 35:29.228
How could she say she only used him
in front of everyone?

35:29.645 --> 35:32.648
Gosh. I hope
he comes around soon enough.

35:36.235 --> 35:37.986
Why don't we set him up
on a blind date?

35:38.070 --> 35:39.363
- Yes.
- That sounds nice.

35:39.446 --> 35:40.656
What do you say, Ms. Yoon?

35:40.739 --> 35:42.449
Is there anyone you know?

35:42.991 --> 35:44.117
He's right.

35:46.245 --> 35:47.621
I don't have friends.

35:48.539 --> 35:49.665
What about any older girls?

35:50.249 --> 35:52.459
It'd be weird
if she were younger than you.

35:52.960 --> 35:54.253
- Think about it.
- Anyone, Ms. Pyun?

35:54.336 --> 35:55.337
No.

36:05.639 --> 36:07.307
I just got on the Olympic Expressway.

36:07.391 --> 36:09.643
I'll be right on the highway
after getting into the interchange.

36:09.893 --> 36:11.853
Okay, I'm already
on the Gyeongbu Expressway

36:11.937 --> 36:13.689
and heading to Seoul.

36:14.731 --> 36:16.692
I'll get off the ramp soon, too

36:16.775 --> 36:18.151
so let's meet at Giheung today.

36:18.527 --> 36:20.654
I'll be at the Mannamui Gwangjang
Service Area in five minutes.

36:20.737 --> 36:22.364
Just give up.

36:23.282 --> 36:24.408
Come on.

36:24.992 --> 36:26.660
I left really early today.

36:28.787 --> 36:35.502
MANNAMUI GWANGJANG SERVICE AREA

36:42.092 --> 36:44.636
Come on. Why do you always
drive so far to come here?

36:44.720 --> 36:46.263
I said I'd come over.

36:46.888 --> 36:48.557
Can't you wait a little
in front of the center?

36:49.683 --> 36:51.768
Or we could meet
at a service area nearer to you.

36:51.852 --> 36:54.438
By then, the northbound expressway
will have less traffic.

36:55.355 --> 36:56.607
Work must be tough enough for you.

36:56.690 --> 36:59.192
I told you not to drive
so far from there.

37:01.403 --> 37:04.615
Anyway, since I lost again,
the snacks are on me.

37:05.907 --> 37:08.160
Then why don't we buy
some sausage and rice cake skewers

37:08.952 --> 37:10.495
and get some rest over there?

37:14.625 --> 37:15.626
What?

37:16.084 --> 37:17.794
Why would you eat skewers over there?

37:20.922 --> 37:22.007
Let's go.

37:44.363 --> 37:46.490
You know what?
I'm seriously starting to get mad.

37:46.907 --> 37:48.408
These files are all confidential

37:48.492 --> 37:50.410
so I couldn't lay them out
in the service area.

37:50.952 --> 37:52.162
In that case

37:52.496 --> 37:55.332
you could've just flatly said
we were coming here to work.

37:55.499 --> 37:57.292
Did you have to give
a flirtatious look and say

37:58.960 --> 38:00.879
"Should we go there?"

38:00.962 --> 38:03.465
My eyes have always been
rather flirtatious.

38:06.802 --> 38:09.763
Gosh, you always need
to do things your way.

38:09.846 --> 38:13.725
Right? You did this when you lied
before the cameras that you used me.

38:13.809 --> 38:15.519
He was just being used.

38:15.602 --> 38:18.063
You also did that when you decided
to move to the logistics center

38:18.146 --> 38:19.481
without telling me.

38:22.025 --> 38:24.486
In-a, just hand in your resignation.

38:24.945 --> 38:27.364
You'll get a disciplinary hearing
and be exiled to some far-off post.

38:27.864 --> 38:29.825
Every step of it will be

38:30.534 --> 38:32.703
devastating and humiliating
to endure.

38:32.786 --> 38:33.829
No.

38:34.204 --> 38:36.123
I will face my consequences
and be disciplined

38:36.206 --> 38:37.916
to take responsibility
for everything I have done.

38:40.252 --> 38:42.921
But I do have one favor
to ask of you, Se-young.

38:44.548 --> 38:45.966
Can you appoint me

38:46.717 --> 38:47.968
to the logistics center?

38:48.427 --> 38:51.096
Joo In-a always has a plan.

38:51.179 --> 38:52.597
It's a plan of her own.

38:52.889 --> 38:54.474
And I'm simply a part of her plan.

38:55.934 --> 38:57.394
Don't say it like that.

38:57.978 --> 38:59.020
A part of my plan?

38:59.730 --> 39:00.772
You are...

39:05.235 --> 39:06.319
a variable.

39:06.903 --> 39:09.239
You're a completely
unexpected lucky variable

39:09.489 --> 39:11.992
which I had never planned for
or even saw coming.

39:14.161 --> 39:15.495
At least you know
how to talk smoothly.

39:32.679 --> 39:34.848
- Was that your father?
- I think the issue with the machine

39:34.931 --> 39:36.224
is due to a defective part.

39:37.142 --> 39:38.810
Are you not going to pick up
his calls now?

39:42.606 --> 39:43.607
Think about it.

39:44.065 --> 39:47.652
From what I overheard last time,
he just wanted a meal with you.

39:58.663 --> 40:00.290
Are you listening?

40:01.208 --> 40:03.084
And why do you keep

40:03.168 --> 40:05.504
picking out the sausages
and giving me the rice cake pieces?

40:05.587 --> 40:08.965
Then there's no point in eating
the sausage and rice cake skewer.

40:09.466 --> 40:11.635
- But I guess it's good.
- That's it!

40:12.636 --> 40:14.095
That might be Jeon Sung-yeol's plan.

40:15.680 --> 40:18.266
He's picking out just the sausages
and keeping only what's good

40:18.809 --> 40:20.477
to throw away the rest.

40:29.110 --> 40:31.404
Let's liquidate five subsidiaries
that are suffering

40:31.488 --> 40:33.073
from structural chronic losses
within this year.

40:34.908 --> 40:35.992
Mr. Vice President.

40:36.076 --> 40:39.329
These subsidiaries
employ a large number of people.

40:39.412 --> 40:42.791
This liquidation will leave
tens of thousands of people jobless.

40:42.874 --> 40:43.917
Mr. Ko.

40:44.251 --> 40:45.627
A business isn't the soup kitchen.

40:45.710 --> 40:47.838
We can't feed those
who don't bring in profit.

40:49.464 --> 40:50.549
Also, Ms. Boo.

40:51.216 --> 40:53.218
What's taking you so long
with the personnel reduction?

40:53.510 --> 40:56.096
Well, there are procedures
I must abide by to do that...

40:56.179 --> 40:58.098
If I were going
to stick to procedures

40:58.181 --> 40:59.891
what do I need you for?

41:00.851 --> 41:02.811
Can you come up with something
more creative?

41:02.894 --> 41:04.604
If we do not abide
by the necessary procedures

41:04.688 --> 41:06.731
it will cause many legal
and management risks...

41:06.815 --> 41:07.983
Exactly.

41:08.441 --> 41:10.569
Isn't the whole point
of paying you good money

41:10.652 --> 41:13.238
to have you manage those risks?

41:17.284 --> 41:18.410
Everyone.

41:18.493 --> 41:19.786
Some tens of thousands
of jobless people

41:19.870 --> 41:21.955
are just a speck of margin of error
in the financial statement.

41:22.664 --> 41:24.207
Stop playing it safe

41:24.666 --> 41:26.126
and earn your keep.

41:27.460 --> 41:28.461
Got it?

41:32.883 --> 41:35.427
Once you sign this paper,
it'll finalize the divorce agreement.

41:39.973 --> 41:42.267
HUSBAND: JEON JAE-YEOL

42:05.290 --> 42:08.752
WIFE

42:19.471 --> 42:20.555
Hyun-young...

42:25.560 --> 42:26.645
Hyun-young.

42:34.486 --> 42:36.279
It's not too late.

42:36.780 --> 42:39.157
You were found innocent
or not guilty or whatever.

42:40.116 --> 42:41.993
That means you aren't guilty.

42:43.119 --> 42:46.289
If you divorce me right now,
you'll literally end up penniless.

42:47.040 --> 42:48.291
Look at your father's condition

42:48.375 --> 42:50.043
and how the company
is in Sung-yeol's hands.

42:52.754 --> 42:54.130
I said I'd help.

42:55.465 --> 42:57.968
I said I'd be your lifeline.
What's wrong with you?

43:05.100 --> 43:06.101
Is it Joo In-a?

43:08.144 --> 43:09.604
It's because of her, right?

43:11.272 --> 43:12.565
It's not that.

43:13.650 --> 43:14.651
You and I

43:15.735 --> 43:17.696
just can't be happy with each other.

43:17.779 --> 43:19.322
What the heck do you know
about my happiness?

43:22.200 --> 43:23.618
I know that I can't give it to you.

43:24.953 --> 43:27.122
So I really want you to find it.

43:28.498 --> 43:30.291
Because I plan to start looking, too.

43:33.378 --> 43:34.504
Jerk.

44:06.077 --> 44:08.246
Line A is stuck again.
Grab the technicians now!

44:08.955 --> 44:10.582
There's not much time left
before shipping.

44:10.915 --> 44:13.126
Darn it. Is it down again?
I can't keep working like this.

44:14.044 --> 44:15.879
This is getting worse and worse.

44:16.254 --> 44:17.464
How was it before?

44:17.547 --> 44:19.174
It wasn't this bad.

44:19.257 --> 44:22.260
After the vice president changed,
the parts supplier also changed.

44:22.343 --> 44:23.511
It's been like this since then.

44:24.262 --> 44:25.346
Where does the shipment

44:26.222 --> 44:27.432
for those parts come into?

45:47.679 --> 45:48.888
Are you okay?

45:50.849 --> 45:53.977
I know it was somewhere here.

45:54.686 --> 45:55.979
Are you looking for something?

45:56.563 --> 45:58.439
No, I thought I dropped something

45:58.648 --> 45:59.899
but I must've been wrong.

46:00.233 --> 46:01.317
Excuse me.

46:35.143 --> 46:36.269
You have reached Moo Kwang-il.

46:37.061 --> 46:38.855
Yes, I understand.
I'll be upstairs soon.

46:43.401 --> 46:44.611
You have reached Cha Sung-tae.

46:45.778 --> 46:47.864
Yes, all right. I'll be upstairs.

46:51.201 --> 46:52.660
This is Baek Hyun-kyu
of Audit Team Three.

46:53.203 --> 46:54.495
Yes, all right.

46:59.209 --> 47:01.502
What were the calls? What's going on?

47:04.964 --> 47:06.841
PERSONNEL RECORD
MOO KWANG-IL

47:06.925 --> 47:09.552
PERSONNEL RECORD
CHA SUNG-TAE

47:13.306 --> 47:15.099
Look at all these people.

47:16.517 --> 47:18.269
What are they all going to do?

47:19.646 --> 47:20.647
Goodness.

47:26.152 --> 47:27.278
Hello, Ms. Boo.

47:27.695 --> 47:29.530
- Have a seat, Mr. Moo.
- Sure.

47:58.017 --> 47:59.602
So our company

48:00.645 --> 48:03.147
is conducting a huge restructuring
and reorganization.

48:03.982 --> 48:05.108
From the Audit Team

48:05.942 --> 48:07.485
they plan to remove
Team Three entirely.

48:09.320 --> 48:10.446
What about us three?

48:11.072 --> 48:14.158
You three will probably get
transferred to another team.

48:21.708 --> 48:24.419
But Mr. Moo, Mr. Cha, and Hyun-kyu...

48:25.878 --> 48:27.046
probably won't...

48:29.590 --> 48:32.260
She'll ask them to retire voluntarily
within a certain period.

48:32.969 --> 48:34.137
If they don't leave in that time

48:34.220 --> 48:35.930
she'll pressure them
by cutting their severance pay.

48:37.098 --> 48:39.851
- That's right.
- This is insane.

48:43.313 --> 48:44.814
What are they going to do?

48:48.401 --> 48:49.485
You see...

48:52.989 --> 48:54.699
As I'd expected,
it was the problem with the parts.

48:55.033 --> 48:56.534
Only the packaging is brand new

48:56.617 --> 48:58.328
and what's inside is all beat-up.

48:58.953 --> 49:01.581
There's no way these new machines
would work smoothly with those.

49:01.664 --> 49:04.167
That would cause a problem
with the logistics process

49:04.250 --> 49:07.003
and the subsidiary, HM Trans,
will drop in its value.

49:07.086 --> 49:08.338
He probably plans to dispose of it.

49:08.796 --> 49:10.715
And the money he gets will be used
to secure his shares.

49:10.798 --> 49:12.759
The headquarters
is slowly downsizing, too.

49:13.259 --> 49:14.886
The restructuring began

49:16.220 --> 49:17.930
and Audit Team Three
will be dissolved.

49:18.431 --> 49:20.641
What? Team Three?

49:21.893 --> 49:24.729
Mr. Moo, Mr. Cha, and even Hyun-kyu

49:24.812 --> 49:26.147
got asked to accept
voluntary retirement.

49:27.065 --> 49:28.316
I wanted to tell you

49:29.192 --> 49:30.401
that I can't come over today.

49:31.235 --> 49:33.071
I think I should be here
with my teammates.

49:35.531 --> 49:36.824
Yes, of course.

49:38.242 --> 49:41.204
Or would you like to come?

49:41.662 --> 49:42.830
They'd all be happy to see you.

49:44.332 --> 49:45.375
Should I do that?

49:57.220 --> 50:01.599
Jeon Sung-yeol has yet to secure
all the shares he needs.

50:01.891 --> 50:04.268
We don't know how it'll play out,
so let's see...

50:04.352 --> 50:05.353
Mr. Noh.

50:08.272 --> 50:11.025
Don't make it sound that easy
just because it's not your business.

50:11.984 --> 50:13.403
What do you mean, you don't know?

50:13.486 --> 50:15.738
We were already notified.

50:16.447 --> 50:17.448
Okay?

50:21.911 --> 50:24.914
Drink slowly.
You're drinking way too fast.

50:25.748 --> 50:26.791
Ms. Pyun.

50:27.834 --> 50:29.293
You must think I'm a joke, too.

50:29.794 --> 50:33.047
Are you going to be stingy
even on a day like this?

50:34.298 --> 50:35.883
- Are you?
- That's not what I mean.

50:36.634 --> 50:38.177
Man. Come on.

50:39.220 --> 50:42.432
- Let me have it. I'll cook the meat.
- It's okay.

50:42.765 --> 50:44.434
- Just let me have it.
- Ms. Yoon!

50:45.226 --> 50:47.937
Cooking meat isn't an easy job.

50:48.020 --> 50:50.565
Don't make it sound like it's easy!

50:54.068 --> 50:57.029
I'm such an incompetent team leader

50:57.864 --> 51:00.366
and I feel too ashamed
to face every one of you.

51:01.701 --> 51:05.580
If I only had a bit of power

51:06.581 --> 51:08.666
I could have stopped

51:09.250 --> 51:10.626
our entire team

51:11.127 --> 51:13.671
from disappearing.

51:14.088 --> 51:17.091
I'm so sorry. I apologize.

51:18.342 --> 51:19.469
Goodness.

51:19.969 --> 51:22.346
What am I going to do now? Gosh.

51:24.390 --> 51:26.350
Oh, goodness.

51:26.893 --> 51:29.020
Thank you for treating us to beef,
Hae-young.

51:29.812 --> 51:31.981
Eat up, and please stop crying.

51:32.607 --> 51:33.608
MS. JOO IN-A

51:33.691 --> 51:36.736
- Where are you?
- Da-yae, will you manage without me?

51:47.830 --> 51:49.415
The word "accomplice"

51:50.333 --> 51:53.044
refers to you and Jeon Sung-yeol.

52:04.931 --> 52:06.891
HAEMU GROUP DISPOSITION PLAN

52:06.974 --> 52:10.645
I'm meeting Mr. Kang of TH,
so book a room at a hostess bar.

52:10.853 --> 52:12.355
And bring in
the right number of partners.

52:14.815 --> 52:18.444
Right. Yes, sir.

52:19.237 --> 52:20.238
What now?

52:20.780 --> 52:21.781
What's with that face?

52:23.324 --> 52:25.868
Wait, has Jae-yeol never asked you
to do something like this?

52:29.789 --> 52:31.207
You know it's just business.

52:31.916 --> 52:33.125
Handle it like a professional.

52:40.299 --> 52:41.425
I see.

52:42.009 --> 52:45.513
I get what you mean, Se-young.
Thank you. Bye.

52:48.558 --> 52:50.893
You said you were nearby,
but you never showed up.

52:52.228 --> 52:53.980
What was that serious call about?

52:54.063 --> 52:55.606
It's Ms. Boo of HR.

52:56.315 --> 52:59.026
I thought we should have someone
on our side at the headquarters

52:59.110 --> 53:01.279
so I compiled everything
I have gathered and sent it to her.

53:01.362 --> 53:03.155
Gosh, it's so cold.

53:03.656 --> 53:07.451
Goodness. It's cold,
so let's go inside and talk later.

53:07.535 --> 53:10.204
Why are you so lightly dressed?
Aren't you cold?

53:10.288 --> 53:12.582
You look colder than I.

53:13.416 --> 53:14.750
Your ears are so red.

53:15.001 --> 53:16.335
I can imagine that.

53:19.297 --> 53:20.548
Ms. Joo?

53:25.177 --> 53:26.304
Ms. Joo!

53:30.266 --> 53:31.392
I must be drunk out of my mind.

53:31.475 --> 53:33.185
Hey, that's our Mr. Noh!

53:33.269 --> 53:34.770
Where have you been?

53:35.021 --> 53:37.064
I've been looking for you.

53:37.773 --> 53:39.191
Is she your girlfriend?

53:39.734 --> 53:42.820
Hello, I'm Mr. Moo,
the incompetent team leader.

53:45.781 --> 53:49.160
Wow, you look just like
Ms. Joo In-a at our workplace.

53:49.243 --> 53:51.412
Hey, look.
She looks just like Ms. Joo!

53:57.460 --> 53:58.628
You're here.

54:02.298 --> 54:03.716
- Come here.
- Hey.

54:12.600 --> 54:15.478
Wait, so who asked whom out?

54:15.561 --> 54:16.979
- I did.
- I did.

54:17.396 --> 54:19.190
What? You two asked each other out?

54:19.273 --> 54:21.859
Look who's in love!

54:22.568 --> 54:26.739
So Ms. Joo's boyfriend
that you once mentioned

54:27.073 --> 54:28.449
was Mr. Noh?

54:29.200 --> 54:31.243
How did you know
who my boyfriend was?

54:31.327 --> 54:33.663
I could tell just by Mr. Noh's eyes.

54:36.332 --> 54:37.375
His eyes?

54:40.419 --> 54:43.172
Hey, Ms. Joo, wait a moment.

54:43.255 --> 54:46.592
What was the thing you said
during the interview?

54:46.676 --> 54:49.095
You said that
you were just using him.

54:50.096 --> 54:51.806
Isn't it obvious?

54:51.889 --> 54:57.478
You told a white lie
for Mr. Noh's sake, isn't that so?

54:57.561 --> 54:59.063
I knew you'd notice, Hae-young.

54:59.980 --> 55:01.816
She was such a romantic!

55:01.899 --> 55:04.568
You two look great together.
I mean it.

55:05.361 --> 55:07.279
You two must be
the best couple there is.

55:08.698 --> 55:09.865
- Are you crying?
- What's with him?

55:09.949 --> 55:11.325
- Why are you crying?
- Yes, why?

55:11.409 --> 55:12.868
- Thanks.
- Gosh.

55:12.952 --> 55:14.745
There's finally a couple
from our Audit Team!

55:14.829 --> 55:19.208
And they're the biggest couple
of this century!

55:22.461 --> 55:25.548
But of course,
I can no longer call it

55:26.006 --> 55:27.633
our Audit Team.

55:31.595 --> 55:33.514
Yes, I shouldn't be so excited

55:34.348 --> 55:35.891
about someone else's love life
right now.

55:37.476 --> 55:38.769
You're right.

55:47.278 --> 55:49.363
The game isn't over yet.

55:50.448 --> 55:51.907
I promised you, didn't I?

55:51.991 --> 55:53.826
That I will be your iron fortress.

55:54.326 --> 55:57.329
And I will keep my promise
until the very end.

56:00.791 --> 56:02.835
Stay strong. It's not over yet!

56:03.711 --> 56:05.838
Your iron fortress stands here!

56:08.758 --> 56:09.925
Thank you!

56:11.343 --> 56:12.636
She's right.

56:18.559 --> 56:22.021
So why did you talk so big
before resolving everything?

56:22.521 --> 56:23.856
I know.

56:24.273 --> 56:26.484
Why am I
so full of myself these days?

56:27.610 --> 56:28.861
I mean, Mr. Moo was

56:29.570 --> 56:32.198
looking at me like this,
so I couldn't just stay still.

56:34.700 --> 56:37.161
I'm glad you did that.
You just have to solve this matter.

56:37.870 --> 56:39.163
- That's right.
- Yes.

56:39.246 --> 56:40.539
I think I can find a way.

56:40.623 --> 56:41.707
Not only is Se-young against him

56:41.791 --> 56:44.251
but there are directors
who are against Jeon Sung-yeol.

56:45.002 --> 56:47.379
In order to convince them
to cast their votes

56:47.922 --> 56:49.882
we need to give them
an alternative to Jeon Sung-yeol.

56:50.382 --> 56:53.719
It has to be someone who has enough
power and trust to go against him

56:53.803 --> 56:57.640
and someone whom the directors
will trust and cast their votes on.

56:59.558 --> 57:00.976
There's only Mr. Jeon Jae-yeol.

57:02.228 --> 57:03.854
Yes, you're right.

57:04.063 --> 57:05.189
But then

57:05.606 --> 57:07.441
we're showing up unannounced.

57:07.733 --> 57:09.819
Do you really think he'll meet us?

57:16.951 --> 57:19.411
I love you.

57:23.040 --> 57:24.875
I love you.

57:37.888 --> 57:39.181
It's called monstera.

57:42.643 --> 57:46.188
Thanks to these holes in the leaves,
the wind can travel easily.

57:46.939 --> 57:49.149
These help them live a long time
without ripping.

57:50.985 --> 57:52.027
That means...

57:54.530 --> 57:55.656
the wounds

57:56.907 --> 57:58.951
are their way of survival.

58:35.154 --> 58:37.698
We're talking about 150,000 people.

58:38.365 --> 58:40.284
If Jeon Sung-yeol sells everything
according to his plan

58:40.367 --> 58:42.328
that's the number of people
who will lose their livelihood.

58:43.704 --> 58:45.456
We have to stop
the worst from happening.

58:46.665 --> 58:48.751
We aren't asking you
to return to the company.

58:48.834 --> 58:51.712
We're just asking you
to help us persuade the directors

58:51.962 --> 58:55.549
so that the board will approve
of Jeon Sung-yeol's dismissal.

58:58.552 --> 59:02.139
In-a, don't you think
you're asking for too much?

59:06.310 --> 59:08.520
You pretended like you were
siding with me in front of the world

59:09.313 --> 59:10.856
to protect your man.

59:11.649 --> 59:14.568
Then you suddenly show up
and ask me to save the company?

59:16.487 --> 59:18.072
I have found my peace.

59:18.656 --> 59:20.240
My mother has become
much better, too.

59:21.367 --> 59:23.118
Please don't get me involved
in this matter.

59:54.358 --> 59:55.567
Did you ask for me?

59:59.905 --> 01:00:01.156
What the heck?

01:00:01.532 --> 01:00:02.574
What did you do?

01:00:02.658 --> 01:00:05.202
Don't you know what it means
to get the right number of partners?

01:00:05.703 --> 01:00:07.121
I did what you asked me to do.

01:00:07.496 --> 01:00:10.416
I invited one employee
per participant to assist them.

01:00:10.499 --> 01:00:12.334
And they were all men!

01:00:14.294 --> 01:00:15.295
You...

01:00:15.963 --> 01:00:17.756
So you can think for yourself.

01:00:18.841 --> 01:00:22.261
I don't need anyone who thinks
and makes their own decision.

01:00:22.344 --> 01:00:24.138
All you need to do
is follow my decisions.

01:00:25.639 --> 01:00:26.724
Get out.

01:00:35.315 --> 01:00:36.483
Hey.

01:00:36.984 --> 01:00:38.610
Hasten the preparation
to sell HM Trans.

01:00:40.571 --> 01:00:42.906
I don't care. Just set the date!

01:00:50.164 --> 01:00:51.206
My dear son.

01:00:52.458 --> 01:00:53.625
Thank you.

01:00:55.002 --> 01:00:56.045
It's still hot.

01:01:17.066 --> 01:01:19.234
We're talking about 150,000 people.

01:01:20.027 --> 01:01:22.696
If Jeon Sung-yeol sells everything
according to his plan

01:01:22.780 --> 01:01:24.698
that's the number of people
who will lose their livelihood.

01:01:36.877 --> 01:01:38.087
SEARCH KEYWORD

01:01:41.340 --> 01:01:42.341
HAEMU GROUP

01:01:43.842 --> 01:01:45.719
RUMORS OF HAEMU SELLING HM TRANS

01:01:49.515 --> 01:01:52.476
HAEMU PLANS TO SELL HM TRANS

01:02:19.378 --> 01:02:20.420
Mr. Vice President!

01:02:20.504 --> 01:02:22.506
This is not a proper way
of selling a company.

01:02:22.589 --> 01:02:24.383
Withdraw the unfair dismissal!

01:02:24.466 --> 01:02:26.385
- Withdraw!
- Withdraw!

01:02:26.468 --> 01:02:28.137
Halt the hasty sell-off!

01:02:28.220 --> 01:02:30.055
- Halt!
- Halt!

01:02:34.059 --> 01:02:35.144
Everyone.

01:02:36.270 --> 01:02:41.024
What you're doing here is considered
obstruction of business. Got it?

01:02:41.108 --> 01:02:42.901
THIS IS NOT RESTRUCTURING, BUT FIRING

01:02:43.694 --> 01:02:46.155
Remove them before my guests arrive.

01:02:49.241 --> 01:02:50.993
- "Remove"?
- Remove us?

01:02:51.618 --> 01:02:52.870
What does he mean by that?

01:02:53.579 --> 01:02:55.497
- Hey, what are you doing?
- You can't do this!

01:03:01.211 --> 01:03:02.880
UNITED WE FIGHT

01:03:11.180 --> 01:03:12.806
Ms. Joo!

01:04:07.110 --> 01:04:10.030
FILING FOR LOVE

01:04:10.656 --> 01:04:13.325
GUEST APPEARANCE BY OH EUI-SHIK

01:04:38.308 --> 01:04:39.685
An emergency board meeting?

01:04:39.768 --> 01:04:41.270
Is he going to dismiss the CEO first?

01:04:41.353 --> 01:04:43.188
- Target found. I'm tailing him.
- Over there.

01:04:43.563 --> 01:04:46.108
Man, it was like
a scene from a movie.

01:04:46.441 --> 01:04:48.068
Wait, a marriage?

01:04:48.151 --> 01:04:49.903
No, I don't do marriages.

01:04:49.987 --> 01:04:51.113
It doubles the risk.

01:04:51.196 --> 01:04:53.323
Not even with me?
Why are you hesitating?

01:04:53.407 --> 01:04:55.701
It feels like they're starting
to swap personalities.

01:04:56.159 --> 01:04:58.453
They say you grow alike
with the one you love.

01:04:58.620 --> 01:04:59.663
Did you just laugh?

01:04:59.746 --> 01:05:02.541
Could there still be
something going on between them?

01:05:03.041 --> 01:05:04.418
I have something to say, Ki-ju.n

01:05:18.307 --> 01:05:20.309
Subtitles by Eunsook Youn
and Jennifer Lim
